{"tool_name":"biocypher","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"biocypher","home":"https://biocypher.org","license":"MIT","summary":"Knowledge graphs (KGs) are an approach to knowledge representation that uses graph structure to facilitate exploration and analysis of complex data, often leveraging semantic information. They are popular in many research areas, including the life sciences, due to their versatile use, for instance in data storage, integration, reasoning, and more recently in artificial intelligence. The creation of KGs is a complex task; BioCypher helps you in creating and maintaining your own KG.","addition_date":"2024-11-05T16:40:31.425701Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-05T16:51:45.184574Z","tool_type":["Library"],"collections":["BioCypher"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:biocypher","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"sebastian.lobentanzer@gmail.com","name":"Sebastian Lobentanzer","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3399-6695","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://slobentanzer.github.io"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://biocypher.org/api.html"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://biocypher.org/index.html"},{"type":["Installation instructions"],"url":"https://biocypher.org/installation.html"},{"type":["Quick start guide"],"url":"https://biocypher.org/quickstart.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"note":"Can ingest arbitrary input formats and creates a number of output formats for in-memory (Python) representation of knowledge graphs as well as database management system representations.","operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"Filtering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3695"},{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"},{"term":"Parsing","uri